course: dictionary
lesson: 4605
title: Hexagon: a six-sided shape
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A hexagon is a flat shape with 6 straight sides and 6 corners. «A triangle has 3 sides and 3 corners, a square 4, a pentagon 5 and a hexagon 6.» Count the sides to check if a shape is a hexagon.
explain: A regular hexagon is special: all 6 sides are the same length and all 6 angles are the same size, 120 degrees each. Look for clue words like «regular» and «all the same» when you read.
explain: You can find hexagons all around you. Bees build honeycomb with hexagon cells, and floor tiles and nuts and bolts are often hexagon-shaped. The word hexagonal means the same as hexagon-shaped.
fact: A hexagon is a flat shape with 6 straight sides and 6 corners.
fact: A regular hexagon has all 6 sides the same length and all 6 angles 120 degrees each.
fact: The angles of a hexagon add up to 720 degrees.
fact: Bees build honeycomb cells as hexagons, which hold the most honey for the least wax.
fact: Snowflakes have six-fold shapes, and Saturn's north pole has a six-sided jet stream called the hexagon.
exercise: «A hexagon has 6 sides.» How many corners does a hexagon have? | 8 | 4 | *6 | 3
exercise: «Honeycomb cells are hexagons, which hold the most honey for the least wax.» What shape are honeycomb cells? | Square | *Hexagon | Circle | Triangle
exercise: «A regular hexagon has all 6 sides the same length and all 6 angles the same size.» What does regular mean here? | *All sides and angles are the same | It has curved sides | It has only 4 corners | It is very big
test: «Six turns of 60 degrees make a hexagon, because the turns add up to one full circle, 360 degrees.» How many degrees go all the way round a full circle? | 180 | *360 | 720 | 90
test: Which word means a flat shape with 6 straight sides and 6 corners? | Cube | Circle | *Hexagon | Pentagon
exam: «Pointy hexagon blocks hold true-or-false answers.» What do the hexagon blocks hold? | Pictures | Numbers | Words | *True-or-false answers
